  "description": "<p>When accessing an object with a historic version, attempting to use the fixty service on the version via the web application generates a namespace error.<br/>\n<a href=\"http://IP:8080/fedora/path/location/object/files/binary/fcr:fixity\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://IP:8080/fedora/path/location/object/files/binary/fcr:fixity</a> <br/>\nfunctions normally for the object.<br/>\nWhen accessing version1 in the versions, using<br/>\n<a href=\"http://IP:8080/fedora/path/location/object/files/binary/fcr:versions/versionid/fcr:fixity\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://IP:8080/fedora/path/location/object/files/binary/fcr:versions/versionid/fcr:fixity</a> <br/>\ngenerates an error.</p>\n\n<p>This has been tested with Fedora 4.7.0 and 4.7.1 on both postgres and the file-simple configuration. </p>\n\n<p>See attached document for the full error displayed on the site.</p>\n\n<p>Tomcat error logs also include the following line:<br/>\nERROR (WildcardExceptionMapper) Exception intercepted by WildcardExceptionMapper: Error converting \"fcr:fixity\" from String to a Name</p>",
